---
description: C++ naming — PascalCase types/functions/namespaces, camelCase variables, ALL_CAPS constants
alwaysApply: true
---

# Naming conventions

Write identifiers like the console overlay below. Do not silently rename existing lowercase folders (`src/core`, `src/maps`, …) unless the team asks.

## Folders — PascalCase

Each new path segment starts uppercase.

- ✅ `Player/`, `SpikeFloor/`, `Maps/House/`
- ❌ `player/`, `spike_floor/`, `maps/house/`

Leave as-is: `build/`, `.cursor`, `.git`, and the existing `src/` tree until renamed on purpose.

## Files

Headers we own use `.hpp`. Implementation stays `.cpp`. No new `.h` for our code.

- ✅ `spike_floor.hpp`, `game_constants.hpp`
- ❌ `spike_floor.h`

File names stay `snake_case` (existing `src/` style). Types and namespaces inside them are still PascalCase.

## Types — PascalCase

Structs, classes, enums. Interfaces prefix `I`.

- ✅ `ConsoleLine`, `PositionPacket`, `IRenderer`
- ❌ `console_line`, `consoleLine`

## Namespaces — PascalCase for a file’s public API

- ✅ `namespace EditorFunctions { void Print(...); }`
- Shared match tunables stay in `namespace hh` (`hh::MAX_PLAYERS`).
- File-private constants, helpers, and state go in an anonymous namespace — not in the public namespace.
- Do not name a namespace `SteamClient` — Steamworks already uses that symbol. Our Steam wrapper is `HhSteam`.

## Functions — PascalCase

- ✅ `UpdateConsole()`, `PushLine()`, `Clamp01()`, `PlaceTrap()`
- ❌ `updateConsole()`, `push_line()`

Raylib APIs already match. Do not wrap them in snake_case helpers.

## Variables, members, parameters — camelCase

No trailing `_` on new members. Mutexes end in `Mutex`.

- ✅ `lifeTime`, `timeLeft`, `deltaTime`, `linesMutex`, `renderer`
- ❌ `LifeTime`, `life_time`, `lifeTime_`, `lines_mutex`

## Constants — ALL_CAPS

Every named constant, including file-local `constexpr` / `const` objects. Never `#define`. Never camelCase.

- ✅ `MAX_LINE_COUNT`, `DEFAULT_LINE_LIFE_TIME`, `TEXT_SCALE`, `hh::BUILD_TIME_SEC`
- ❌ `maxLineCount`, `defaultLineLifeTime`

Members stay camelCase even when initialized from a constant (`lifeTime = DEFAULT_LINE_LIFE_TIME`).

## Pointers, refs, const

Attach `*` and `&` to the type. `const` on anything the callee does not mutate. Primitives by value; objects by `const T&`.

- ✅ `const std::string& text`, `const Vector3& color`, `const float deltaTime`, `IRenderer* renderer`
- ❌ `const Vector3 &color`, `const char *name`, `float DeltaTime`

```cpp
namespace {
constexpr int MAX_LINE_COUNT = 10;
constexpr float DEFAULT_LINE_LIFE_TIME = 8.0f;
const Vector3 DEFAULT_COLOR{255.0f, 255.0f, 255.0f};

struct ConsoleLine {
    std::string text;
    Vector3 color = DEFAULT_COLOR;
    float lifeTime = DEFAULT_LINE_LIFE_TIME;
    float timeLeft = DEFAULT_LINE_LIFE_TIME;
};

std::deque<ConsoleLine> lines;
std::mutex linesMutex;

void PushLine(const std::string& text, const Vector3& color, const float lifeTime) { /* ... */ }
}

namespace EditorFunctions {
void Print(const std::string& text);
void UpdateConsole(const float deltaTime);
void RenderConsole(IRenderer* renderer);
}
```
